.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt AWK 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm awk
.Nd pattern-directed scanning and processing (bounded POSIX core)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl F Ar fs
.Op Fl v Ar name=value
.Op Fl f Ar program-file
.Ar program
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility applies pattern-action rules to records read from the input files.
The supported core includes:
.Bl -bullet
.It
records and fields
.Pq Va $0 .. $NF ,
.Fl F
and
.Va FS ;
.It
.Va BEGIN
and
.Va END
rules;
.It
arithmetic, comparison, logical and regex-match operators, string concatenation and variables;
.It
associative arrays and
.Ic for ( Ns Ar k Ic in Ar a Ns Ic ) ;
.It
.Ic if/else , while
and C-style
.Ic for ;
.It
.Ic print , printf , length , substr , index , split , sub , gsub , match ,
.Ic sprintf
and
.Ic int ;
.It
.Va NR , NF , FS , OFS
and
.Va ORS .
.El
.Pp
User-defined functions, `getline`, pipes, `close`, `system`, output redirection, full regex
escapes and unlisted built-ins are not implemented and are usage errors.
The target image currently requires file operands; standard input is a follow-up.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 2 for an invalid/unsupported program or an I/O error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr grep 1 ,
.Xr sed 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
